**Reused evidence**
None. There are no previously accepted web evidence IDs in-thread to reuse; I used the local prior only as the starting baseline.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran (Islamic Republic of) 1979 (rev. 1989) Constitution","publisher":"Constitute Project","publication_date":"1989-07-28","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Iran_1989","claim":"Article 110 gives the Leader supreme command of the armed forces, war-and-peace authority, and appointment power over key judiciary, media, and military posts; Article 111 provides a temporary replacement council if the office becomes vacant.","locator":"Articles 110-111","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Stable constitutional text reproduced by a reputable legal repository; directly defines authority and constraints relevant to 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Enduring constitutional baseline governing 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct office-level authority held by Ali Khamenei as Supreme Leader.","contrary_evidence":["The constitution includes a formal vacancy-replacement mechanism, so the office is powerful but not literally unbounded on paper."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.7","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran not seeking nuclear weapons, needs atomic energy, says Khamenei","publisher":"Voice of America (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-02-17","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/iran-not-seeking-nuclear-weapons-084757433.html","claim":"Khamenei said Iran needed peaceful nuclear energy and denied seeking nuclear weapons while supporting Vienna diplomacy on sanctions relief.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted speech excerpt","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire story distributed by VOA; direct contemporaneous quotation but not a primary transcript.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler statement during the JCPOA talks","ruler_attribution":"Direct attribution to Khamenei in his role as supreme leader.","contrary_evidence":["The same year, Iran curtailed inspections and expanded enrichment to 60% under IAEA monitoring reports."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Khamenei Says Iran's Future Should Not Be Tied to Nuclear Talks","publisher":"Voice of America (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-04-13","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/khamenei-says-iran-s-future-should-not-be-tied-to-nuclear-talks-/6528929.html","claim":"Khamenei said Iran's future should not depend on the success or failure of nuclear talks and told officials not to let work stall because of negotiations.","locator":"opening paragraph and quoted speech excerpt","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire distributed by VOA; direct quote from the ruler in the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler statement during stalled Vienna talks","ruler_attribution":"Direct attribution to Khamenei.","contrary_evidence":["This rhetoric was paired later in 2022 with reduced monitoring and additional enrichment steps."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Khamenei adviser says Tehran 'capable of building nuclear bomb' - Reuters","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-07-18","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/07/18/us-iran-nuclear-usa","claim":"Kamal Kharrazi, described as a senior adviser to Khamenei, said Iran had the technical capability to build a nuclear bomb but had not decided whether to do so.","locator":"Reuters story opening paragraph and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire through Euronews; reliable as a report of a close adviser, but attribution to Khamenei is indirect.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Mid-2022 context for the leader's nuclear orbit","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution through a senior adviser to the Supreme Leader.","contrary_evidence":["This is not a direct Khamenei statement and does not prove an actual decision to weaponize."],"lenses":["1B.6","1B.7","1B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Statement by the Vice-President of Iran and the IAEA Director General","publisher":"International Atomic Energy Agency","publication_date":"2022-03-06","url":"https://www.iaea.org/es/newscenter/pressreleases/declaracion-conjunta-del-excmo-sr-mohammad-eslami-vicepresidente-y-presidente-de-la-organizacion-de-energia-atomica-del-iran-y-el-excmo-sr-rafael-grossi-director-general-del-organismo-internacional-de-energia-atomica","claim":"Iran's atomic energy organization agreed to provide written explanations and supporting documents on three undeclared locations by March 20, 2022, with follow-up meetings in Tehran and a goal of reporting conclusions by the June 2022 Board meeting.","locator":"numbered items 1-4 in the joint statement","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IAEA text with explicit dates, obligations, and follow-up steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 safeguards process surrounding Khamenei's nuclear posture","ruler_attribution":"Institutional Iran-side commitment under the Supreme Leader's system; not a personal order from Khamenei on the page, but directly relevant to his authority over the file.","contrary_evidence":["The same issue later remained unresolved, showing the March process did not close the safeguards gap."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.7","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Verification and monitoring in the Islamic Republic of Iran in light of UNSCR 2231 (2015)","publisher":"International Atomic Energy Agency","publication_date":"2022-05-30","url":"https://www.isis-online.org/uploads/iaea-reports/documents/gov2022-24.pdf","claim":"The IAEA reported that Iran continued enriching uranium up to 60% U-235 and that its JCPOA-related verification and monitoring were seriously affected after Iran stopped implementing its nuclear-related commitments, including the Additional Protocol.","locator":"pp. 3-4, paras. 15-17 and 51-55","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct IAEA report in the target year with specific operational findings and monitoring consequences.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 reporting period","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is to the Iranian state under Khamenei's top-level authority over the nuclear file.","contrary_evidence":["Iran maintained that its program was peaceful and that pressure from the West drove the rollback.","The report documents state-level actions, not a private decision transcript from Khamenei."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.3","1B.4","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran Turns off Twenty-Seven Cameras","publisher":"Iran Watch / IAEA report reproduction","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://www.iranwatch.org/library/multilateral-organizations/international-atomic-energy-agency/iaea-report/iran-turns-twenty-seven-cameras-verification-monitoring-islamic","claim":"Iran ordered removal of IAEA surveillance cameras and related equipment; the Director General said this removed the possibility for full confidence in future declarations and could damage assurance of the peaceful nature of Iran's nuclear program.","locator":"paras. 5-9","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The page reproduces the contemporaneous IAEA report and captures the agency's direct assessment of the consequences.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 operational decision affecting monitoring continuity","ruler_attribution":"State action under Khamenei's top-level control over the nuclear file; not a personal directive on the page.","contrary_evidence":["Iran framed the move as a response to IAEA behavior rather than a reduction in safety.","The action preserved seals and storage, but still degraded continuity of knowledge."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.8","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Verification and monitoring in the Islamic Republic of Iran in light of UNSCR 2231 (2015)","publisher":"International Atomic Energy Agency","publication_date":"2022-11-10","url":"https://www.iranwatch.org/sites/default/files/gov2022-62.pdf","claim":"After the June camera removal, the IAEA said it could not recover continuity of knowledge and could not exclude that subsequent levels of activity were significantly different from what had previously been observed.","locator":"pp. 2-3, paras. 6-11","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IAEA reporting with direct statement about the monitoring gap created in 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 reporting period","ruler_attribution":"Institutional consequence of decisions taken under Khamenei's authority over the nuclear portfolio.","contrary_evidence":["The IAEA said a new baseline could eventually be established, but only after a considerable time and with uncertainty."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.8","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran sets up meeting on IAEA inquiry as diplomatic clash looms","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-11-11","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/11/iran-nuclear-iaea","claim":"Iran agreed to a November IAEA visit to start giving answers on uranium particles found at three sites, though diplomats said the move came before an expected new Board resolution.","locator":"opening paragraph and Reuters summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on an explicit diplomatic step, but still mediated through a secondary publisher.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 response to the safeguards dispute","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is to the Iranian government and nuclear authorities under Khamenei's system, not a personal Khamenei speech.","contrary_evidence":["Diplomats described the visit as possibly tactical rather than a substantive breakthrough."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IAEA board passes resolution ordering Iran to cooperate with probe","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-11-18","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/18/iran-nuclear-iaea","claim":"The IAEA Board of Governors passed a resolution ordering Iran to cooperate urgently with the probe into uranium traces at three undeclared sites.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire on a major multilateral response, useful for chronology and external pressure but not a primary IAEA document itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 escalation point in the safeguards dispute","ruler_attribution":"Institutional consequence for Iran's nuclear policy under Khamenei's authority.","contrary_evidence":["The resolution is an external rebuke, not evidence that Khamenei personally issued the underlying nuclear decisions."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran starts enriching uranium to 60% purity at Fordow site - official","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters wire)","publication_date":"2022-11-23","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/23/iran-nuclear","claim":"Iran began enriching uranium to 60% at Fordow after the Board resolution, a step described as retaliation to pressure from the IAEA and Western powers.","locator":"opening paragraphs and Reuters explanation of the timing","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with a direct, contemporaneous account of the new enrichment step and its stated trigger.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate late-2022 escalation after multilateral censure","ruler_attribution":"State-level nuclear escalation under Khamenei's top-level authority over the file.","contrary_evidence":["Iran presented the move as a response to political pressure, not a move toward weaponization.","The report does not prove a direct Khamenei order, only state action under his system."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4","1B.9","1B.10"]}

Taken together, the chapter is strongest on a simple pattern: Khamenei's public rhetoric in February and April 2022 stayed within a non-apocalyptic, negotiation-aware line, but the verifiable operational record moved in the opposite direction. The decisive 2022 negatives are the 60% enrichment trajectory, the suspension of Additional Protocol-style transparency, the June camera removal, and the late-year inability of the IAEA to preserve continuity of knowledge.

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across these families: IAEA 2022 reports (`GOV/2022/4`, `GOV/2022/24`, `GOV/2022/26`, `GOV/2022/62`, `GOV/INF/2022/14`), UN Security Council record pages for the same reports, Reuters wire stories syndicated by VOA/Euronews/Yahoo/KFGO/The National/RT, the constitution text, the Library of Congress archive for `leader.ir`, IRNA archive pages, Tasnim/Fars searches, World Nuclear News, Washington Post, Axios, and Al Jazeera.

I rejected:
- Duplicate syndications of the same Reuters wire story when they added no new fact.
- Broad background pages that were not materially specific to 1B or not about 2022.
- Older Khamenei fatwa / historical nuclear-doc material from 2012-2019 except as background context, because the user asked for 2022 research.
- Post-2022 retrospectives and 2026 conflict coverage, because they fall outside the target period.
- Generic human-rights or macroeconomic sources that were already covered by the local prior and did not add 1B-specific nuclear-risk evidence.
- Official `leader.ir` access attempts that did not surface a stable, directly usable 2022 English transcript in the accessible search results.
- IRNA/Tasnim/Fars searches that did not yield a stable 2022 Persian nuclear transcript distinct enough from the Reuters/IAEA evidence to retain here.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct Persian-language 2022 Khamenei transcript on the nuclear file or JCPOA line. I found the source family, but not a stable, uniquely useful article worth retaining.
- Better primary evidence on 1B.7, especially who Khamenei relied on for nuclear-risk expertise and whether he elevated technocrats or ideologues in 2022.
- Better direct evidence on 1B.6, meaning explicit restraint against proliferation by proxies or domestic factions. The current record is mostly indirect.
- Better crisis-channel evidence for 1B.8 beyond the IAEA dialogue and the late-2022 tactical visit offer.
- If you want more saturation, further search would help most on those three weak lenses; it would probably only modestly change the already strong 1B.3, 1B.4, 1B.9, and 1B.10 picture.
